  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14223345/assets/06c6dd24948a95d08850455d273c3456076850a47c980a086f06813b96bfd6ed.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero",
